# AUR packages. These are NOT installed by pacstrap (the base install has no AUR
# helper). They are built via an AUR helper during post-install: online-only and
# best-effort, so the install completes without them and they arrive later.
# One package per line; '#' and blank lines are ignored. Use the AUR PackageBase.

# AUR helper (bootstrapped first so the rest can be built)
yay-bin


# Cursor themes: extra XCursor themes the Ryoku Settings picker offers on top of
# the configured default. Bibata (XCURSOR_THEME defaults to Bibata-Modern-Ice)
# now ships first-class from the [ryoku] repo as a hard ryoku-desktop dependency,
# not the AUR: an AUR-only theme installed only in the post-install step (skipped
# offline, best-effort on failure) and `ryoku update` never revisited it, so a
# box could come up with no configured cursor. See release/packages/ryoku-cursors.
# The modern flat vimix set ships from the official repo, see base.packages.
# These prebuilt extras are best-effort, like every package in this set.
# phinger: clean rounded set, light and dark, from a prebuilt release.
phinger-cursors
# volantes intentionally omitted: it renders its cursors from SVG via inkscape
# with no prebuilt release, so it cannot bake headless in CI. The desktop still
# ships Bibata, vimix, phinger, catppuccin and apple cursor sets.
# catppuccin (Mocha): soft pastel set with several accent variants.
catppuccin-cursors-mocha
# apple_cursor (macOS style): builds from source via clickgen, so it can be slow or
# fail to build; best-effort, like every package in this set.
apple_cursor

# Wallpaper daemon: Ryogami now ships first-class from the [ryoku] repo as a hard
# ryoku-desktop dependency (see release/packages/ryogami/PKGBUILD). It supersedes
# awww (the retired swww fork); no wallpaper daemon comes from the AUR anymore.

# NVIDIA digital vibrance for the pill mixer's DISPLAY saturation fader, on
# Wayland (ioctls on /dev/nvidia-modeset). AUR-only; a no-op on non-NVIDIA GPUs.
nvibrant-bin

# LocalSend: AirDrop-style LAN file sharing; the pill's file stash speaks its protocol.
localsend-bin

# GlazePKG (gpk) ships first-class from the [ryoku] repo now, not the AUR.

# Speech-to-text for the pill Super+` voice dictation (tap-to-toggle + mic wave).
# Voxtype is an offline Whisper daemon the shell drives via `voxtype record`; it
# ships every engine (Whisper + the ONNX set) and types through wtype.
voxtype-bin

# Display + UI fonts for the Ryoku brand type stack: Fraunces (variable serif,
# editorial headlines). Space Grotesk (the UI sans) now ships from the [ryoku]
# repo (base.packages + release/packages/otf-space-grotesk) because its AUR
# pkgbase builds from source with fontforge and failed headless in the ISO CI.
# Inter, JetBrains Mono and Noto ship from the official repo (base.packages).
ttf-fraunces-variable

# Web browser: Zen is the AUR option in the installer's one-browser choice;
# Firefox is recommended and selected by default. Zen builds post-install on an
# online install and is baked into the ISO's offline repo. Existing boxes are
# not given Zen by an update, but a user who installs it themselves still gets
# the Ryoku Zen policy (shipped extensions plus Wayland, hardware-decode and
# privacy defaults) from `ryoku doctor`. See reconcile_zen.go.
zen-browser-bin

# Fingerprint unlock module. The in-session lock (qylock) and the SDDM greeter
# authenticate through a PAM stack that loads pam_fprintd_grosshack.so, which
# forks fprintd-verify at the start of the conversation so the sensor scans while
# the password field is live (touch OR type, whichever lands first). fprintd's
# own enroll/verify (Ryoku Settings) works without it, but the lock/greeter
# fingerprint path silently does nothing when the module is absent. AUR-only, so
# it lands on new installs here; reconcileFingerprintModule backfills existing
# boxes that have a reader (this set is not revisited by `ryoku update`).
pam-fprint-grosshack
